{"repositoryId":418503284,"availability":"available","full":"leggedrobotics/rsl_rl","name":"rsl_rl","description":"A fast and simple implementation of learning algorithms for robotics.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":3074,"forks":697,"created":"2021-10-18T13:00:35Z","updated":"2026-10-12T15:26:34Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://leggedrobotics.github.io/rsl_rl/","topics":[],"demo":"https://leggedrobotics.github.io/rsl_rl/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T15:55:15.887Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T15:55:15.887Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T15:55:15.887Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T17:01:04.061Z","stars":3065,"forks":697},{"at":"2026-10-19T15:55:15.887Z","stars":3074,"forks":697}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["RSL-RL is a GPU-accelerated, lightweight learning library for robotics research. Its compact design allows researchers to prototype and test new ideas without the overhead of modifying large, complex libraries. RSL-RL can also be used out-of-the-box by installing it via PyPI, supports multi-GPU training, and features common algorithms for robot learning.","Additional algorithms, models, and more, mainly contributed by the community, can be found on the extras branch. This allows us to keep the core library on main minimal and easy to start with. To see a list of the additional features, please check the Extras Documentation."],"features":["Minimal, readable codebase with clear extension points for rapid prototyping.","Robotics-first methods including PPO and Student-Teacher Distillation.","High-throughput training with native Multi-GPU support.","Proven performance in numerous research publications."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/leggedrobotics/rsl_rl/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2cc91a5d8c1b1c4d6f0da291153373d9b39df1b67ec10f10cee54027de010e19","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:04.111Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:04.111